Remark I.1. The choice of TLA⁺ for O1–O3, O8–O9 and Isabelle for O4–O7 reflects the content: the discrete skeleton (states, transitions, authority resolution, induction) is TLA-shaped, while the parametric inequalities (7), (8) are linear arithmetic over $\mathbb{Q}$, which Isabelle handles exactly. With rational parameters, $B(t)$ remains rational at every $t$ and comparisons are decidable, so no rounding refinement is required for the theorems as stated. Apalache supports inductive invariant checking with SMT over unbounded integers and is the appropriate first tool for O1–O3 and O8–O9; TLAPS and Isabelle are appropriate for O4–O7.

